<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Madison returns after completing all twelve psychotherapy sessions. Since his preventive visit ten weeks ago he has had one event, during his stomach illness five weeks ago, and none since; he recognizes the warning feeling earlier and uses his grounding steps. He has taken sertraline 50 mg each morning for fifteen weeks, apart from two days missed when he was vomiting; he has no side effects now. The nurse telephone check planned two weeks after starting sertraline did not take place. His mood is steadier and he worries less; he sat the law school admission test last week with extra breaks and felt he did himself justice. He has gone back to evening civic meetings with a friend who knows the first-aid plan. He has not driven and asks when he may. He has had no thoughts of death or self-harm, and the rifle remains locked. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Events</td><td>One in ten weeks, during an acute illness; none for five weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Psychotherapy</td><td>Twelve of twelve sessions completed; relapse-prevention plan written</td></tr><tr><td>Sertraline</td><td>50 mg for fifteen weeks; no side effects now</td></tr><tr><td>PHQ-9 and GAD-7</td><td>6 and 7</td></tr><tr><td>Driving</td><td>Not driving; asks when he may</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

